        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Plants: Anemopaegma, Pithecoctenium, Bignonia\n- Mythology figures: Semele, Dionysus, Zeus, Cadmus, Harmonia\n- Topics: Bignoniaceae, Greek mythology\n\nFacts:\n- Anemopaegma is a genus of flowering plants in the family Bignoniaceae.\n- In Greek mythology, Semele was the daughter of the Boeotian hero Cadmus and Harmonia.\n- In Greek mythology, Semele was the mortal mother of Dionysus by Zeus in one of his many origin myths.\n- Pithecoctenium is a genus closely related to Bignonia and Anemopaegma.",
